{"name":"Golden Harvest","hex":"#cccc11","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"golden","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of, or relating to, gold.","Having a color or other richness suggestive of gold."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["(Can we verify this sense?) brassy drummer, brassy chub, etc. (Kyphosus vaigiensis), a fish found in southeast Asia.","Ellipsis of golden retriever."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/golden"},{"term":"harvest","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The process of gathering the ripened crop; harvesting.","The yield of harvesting, i.e., the gathered crops or fruits."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To bring in a harvest; reap; glean.","To take a living organism as part of a managed process to gather food or resources, often with the intention of maintaining a healthy population."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/harvest"}],"entries":[{"title":"Orange Sky Golden Harvest","blocks":[{"text":"Orange Sky Golden Harvest (OSGH), previously known as Golden Harvest Entertainment Group from 1970 to 2009, is a film production, distribution, and exhibition company based in Hong Kong. It dominated Hong Kong cinema box office sales from the 1970s to the 1980s, and played a major role in introducing Hong Kong action films to the world, especially those by Bruce Lee, Jackie Chan, Jet Li, and Sammo Hung."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/4/49/Golden_Harvest_on_screen_logo_%281978-1999%29.jpg/330px-Golden_Harvest_on_screen_logo_%281978-1999%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orange_Sky_Golden_Harvest","wikidata":"Q541569"},{"title":"The Golden Harvest","blocks":[{"text":"The Golden Harvest is a Brazilian Modernist novel. It was written by Jorge Amado from 1942 to 1944, published in Portuguese in 1944 and in English in 1992."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/fb/S%C3%A3oJorgeDosIlh%C3%A9us.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Golden_Harvest","wikidata":"Q154675"},{"title":"Golden Harvest (book)","blocks":[{"text":"Golden Harvest is a 2011 book about the Holocaust in Poland. It was written by historians Jan T. Gross and Irena Grudzińska-Gross. It was first published in Polish in March 2011, with an English translation following in 2012."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/71/Golden_Harvest_book_cover.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Golden_Harvest_(book)","wikidata":"Q9393423"},{"title":"Harvest","blocks":[{"text":"Harvesting is the process of collecting plants, animals, or fish as food, especially the process of gathering mature crops, and \"the harvest\" also refers to the collected crops. Reaping is the cutting of grain or pulses for harvest, typically using a scythe, sickle, or reaper. On smaller farms with minimal mechanization, harvesting is the most labor-intensive activity of the growing season. On large mechanized farms, harvesting uses farm machinery, such as the combine harvester. Automation has increased the efficiency of both the seeding and harvesting processes. Specialized harvesting equipment, using conveyor belts for gentle gripping and mass transport, replaces the manual task of removing each seedling by hand. The term \"harvesting\" in general usage may include immediate postharvest handling, including cleaning, sorting, packing, and cooling."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Agriculture_in_Volgograd_Oblast_002.JPG/330px-Agriculture_in_Volgograd_Oblast_002.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Harvest","wikidata":"Q213753"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/GH_Grand_Ocean.JPG/500px-GH_Grand_Ocean.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/GH_Grand_Ocean.JPG/1280px-GH_Grand_Ocean.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/GH_Grand_Ocean.JPG/500px-GH_Grand_Ocean.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Entrance to Grand Ocean Cinema at Harbour City","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGH_Grand_Ocean.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Z%C5%82ote_%C5%BCniwa-Treblinka_fotografia.jpg/500px-Z%C5%82ote_%C5%BCniwa-Treblinka_fotografia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Z%C5%82ote_%C5%BCniwa-Treblinka_fotografia.jpg/1280px-Z%C5%82ote_%C5%BCniwa-Treblinka_fotografia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Z%C5%82ote_%C5%BCniwa-Treblinka_fotografia.jpg/500px-Z%C5%82ote_%C5%BCniwa-Treblinka_fotografia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Photo printed in a 2008 article, \"Gorączka złota w Treblince\" (\"Gold Rush in Treblinka\") by Gazeta Wyborcza journalists Marcin Kowalski and Piotr Głuchowski. The photo served as an inspiration for Gross' Golden Harvest and was reprinted on his book's cover. The nature of the supposed diggers has been disputed by scholars.  ","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AZ%C5%82ote_%C5%BCniwa-Treblinka_fotografia.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Harvest_Straw_Bales_in_Schleswig-Holstein.jpg/500px-Harvest_Straw_Bales_in_Schleswig-Holstein.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.